   "widgets_values": [
    "HaDeS MOSS Suite - Merge Lab (advanced)\n\nMake two merges, judge them blind against their parents, keep the winner as a 3.96 GB file.\n\n1. Merges of SFT (MOSS Loader) and Base (Load Diffusion Model):\n   - Block Merger: the sixth video's TEST recipe, not a recommendation: half of Base in layers 18-35.\n   - Multi-Model Merger: SLERP, equal weights.\n   Change the sliders or the method: that is the experiment.\n2. MOSS Compare Sampler, blind: SFT (A), Base (B), Block Merger (C), SLERP (D) shuffled and numbered on one\n   sheet with the same prompt, seed and settings. Pick your favourite before you look at the key: it is in\n   the _key.json next to the sheet (output/MOSS/merge_lab), never on the sheet. The key names each merge\n   by how it was made: 'merge (blocks 18-35 x0.5): ...' and 'merge (SLERP): ...'.\n   Suite Telemetry reads the loader, the enhancer and both mergers, not the sheet, so it does not reveal the key.\n3. (muted) Keep the winner: MOSS Model Saver in HMS v1, calibrated on the merge itself, with the merger's\n   recipe in the file; connect the winning merger to model and recipe. Then the Metadata Reader reads it back.\n\nMeasured (RTX 5090, tools/RESULTS.md): the blind sheet about 61 s (87 s with the first load).\nSeed 1013, distance at 512 px (0-255): SFT - Base 48.2; the test recipe 34.3 from SFT, 41.2 from Base;\nSLERP 35.1 from SFT, 40.6 from Base; the two merges 9.6 apart (seed 1014: 32.2).\nHMS v1 of the test recipe: 7.6 min, 3.96 GB, 6.1 s an image against 13.3 s live. Against the live merge it kept\nthe scene on both seeds tried; on one the fisherman himself changed (glasses, a longer beard). Put the file in\nmodels/diffusion_models and compare it with the live merge in a Compare Sampler before you keep it."
   ],
   "properties": {}
  }
